Go toolchain

Install:
  Install the latest stable Go release if needed; verify the archive and create missing command links.

Upgrade:
  Update the Go toolchain in ~/.local/share/go to the latest stable release with checksum verification.

Status:
  Report the locally available Go version.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access. Supported architectures: amd64 and arm64.

Configuration:
  Installation directory: ~/.local/share/go
  Missing command links are created in ~/.local/bin; existing user entry points are preserved.
  GOBIN defaults to ~/.local/bin only when unset; existing values are preserved.
  GOENV must allow persistent Go configuration.
